        <p>OP USEFUL &amp; SEASONABLE ARTICLES, • In the MEMORIAL BUILDINGS. THURSDAY, DECEMBER 16th, 1915, CROCKERY STALL. REFRESHMENTS.</p>
        <p>MUSIC. To commence at 3 p.m. Admission 6d.</p>
        <p>B OLD-STREET WESLEYA 24 CHURCH _TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). DEC. 12th.</p>
        <p>Morning, 10.30: Rev. P. Subject: "Daybreak." Evening, 6.30: Rev. W. T. DERRY, M.A.</p>
        <p>142EWSEY-ROAD WESLEYAN CHURCH, TO.MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12th. Morning, 10.30: Mr. J. W. SHERLOCK.' Subject: "The Disciples' Test." Evening. 6.30: Rev. A. J. MORTON. Subject: " Devil's Devices."</p>
        <p>BAPTIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12th.</p>
        <p>Morning, 10.30. Evening. 6. Preacher: Rev. J. W. EDWARDS (Tipton).</p>
        <p>CiAIRO-STREET, CHAPEL, WA IZ RINGTON TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12th.</p>
        <p>Preacher: Rev. IRVINE LISTER. Morning. 10.30. Evening. 6.30.</p>
        <p>OHRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, ‘4-1 BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON.--Free Bible Address SUNDAY NEXT, at 6.30 p.m. Subject: " The Bible Doctrine of the Kingdom of God. The Great Scheme of Human Redemption." Mr. W. STEWART, of Dioylsden. 4'4 OLBORNE STREET BAPTIST CHURCH. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12th. MEMORIAL SERVICES. for the late Sergt.-Major Davies. Preacher: Rev. H. OGDEN. Morning, 10.45. Evening, 6.30. The MAYOR (Ald. Peter Peacock) and a detach- ment of 4th S. Lancs. Regt. will be present at the evening service. Soloist: MDE. SARA SILCOCR. _ _ PREILITIVE METHODIST CHURCH, LEGH-STREET, WARRINGTON. , TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12th, 1915. A Morning, 10.30: M't. A. LUMB. Afternoon, at 2.90: Part 1 of " The Messiah." Evening, 6.30: Part 2 and S of "The Messiah." Soloists: Mrs. C. WORTHINGTON, Mrs. A. E. HOYLE, Miss JESSIE WOODLAND, Miss M AUD JONES, Mr. T. GOOSTREY, Mr. E. H. PEA.RCE. Organist: Mr..F. H. BANNER. Conductor: Mr. A. SPRUCE. , DEFORMED CHURCH OP 'ENGLAND, EMMANUEL CHURCH, BOLD-STREET, Services every SUNDAY. at 10.30 a.m. &amp; 6.30 p.m. Rev. W. T. JAYE, Incumbent. The Church provides a distinctly Protestant Church of Enekind serv.ice. All Seats Free. ,</p>
        <p>QT. JOHN'S' PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH, ST WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). DEC. 12th, 1915. Morning, 10.45. Evening. 6.30. Preacher: • Rev. W. REID. Ordination and Communion Services in the Evening Fri IE SALVATION ARMY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 12, 1915. COMMISSIONER EDWARD J. HIGGINS. In the PICTUREDROME, SANKEY-STREET. 11 a.m. and 6.45 p.m. SALVATION. 3 p.ni., "THE SALVATION ARMY. /N PEACE &amp; WAR." Chairman: HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR (Alderman Peter Peacock). Admission Free. Song Sheets Provided.</p>
