        <p>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Birth</p>
        <p>BEBRINGTON.—On December 9, at 64. West- street, Warrington, to Mr. George Bebbington and Mrs. Bebbington (nee Wilkinson), a son.</p>
        <p>lltri lii t , Marriage. ;i WEIR---ALLMAN.---On the 4th inst., at ,Legh- , street Primitive Methodist Chapel, by the Rev. k 1 4 A. J. Chessum, Corporal Edwin Weir, son of Lawrence Weir, of 22, Arthur-street, to Lily I i Mabel Allman, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. J. Allman, of 55, Legh-street. I</p>
        <p>Deaths.</p>
        <p>BAKER.—On the oth inst., at Walton Crescent, after a brief illness, Clara, widow of the 'late Samuel James Baker, and beloved daughter of Alfred and Elizabeth Tilling, aged 40 years. In- terment at Warrington Cemetery to-day (Satur- day), at 2.15 p.m. . •</p>
        <p>BIRCHALL.—On Decemher 7th, at 12, Bridgewater- street, Warrington, Hannah. the devoted wife of John,, and beloved mother of Mary, Annie and Tom Birchall, aged 66 years. Late of Stockton Heath.</p>
