      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-12-11_WidnesExaminer_art0251" n="art0251">
        <head>BEWSEY ADULT SCHOOL v. LONGFORD ADULT SCHOOL.</head>
        <p>BEWSEY ADULT SCHOOL v. LONGFORD ADULT SCHOOL.</p>
        <p>A grand evening was spent on Tuesday at Bewsey, when the visitors came off best. Referee, R. Williams, of Sankey. Scores : Bewsey.—H. Perks 75, R. Healey 75, J. Mather 75, G. Boyle 75, G. Stockton 43, C. Starkey 69; total 412. Longford.—N. Ellam G. Hughes 3, D. Elwell 50, F. Ellsmore 66, H. Smart 75, J. Smart 75-364—tart 60; total 424. Majority for Longford, 12.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-12-11_WidnesExaminer_art0252" n="art0252">
        <head>NO FALTERING.</head>
        <p>NO FALTERING.</p>
        <p>Sir Arthur Haworth's Advice T 6 The</p>
        <p>Churches.</p>
        <p>Sir Arthur Haworth, the chairman of the Congregational Union of England and Wales, speaking at Heywood last Saturday, said these were times of stress and difficulty. This greatest of crises was not of our seeking, but was thrust upon us as a Christian nation, and we were called upon to strain every nerve for the cause for which we stood, which down on its bedrock principles was the cause of Christianity against a ruthless nation. We had to do all in our power to stand by the right, supporting th,t Government in work and in money, whether we liked it or not. One of the ways in which we could support the Government was by main- taining a noble and courageous spirit, not falter- ing, never doubting, knowing that with God's help and our oivn spirit and sacrifice and effort the right would prevail. The. best means by which a noble spirit could be maintained was that the churches, all sections of Christ's church, should be vigorous and hearty in 'their work in the country, sustaining their members and encouraging and exhorting and sympathis- ing with the people, for sympathy was much</p>
        <p>Sugar alone will sustain life for a consider- able time.</p>
        <p>Time is money. Like tide, it waits for no man. \</p>
      </div>
